# Environment variables. Copy this file to .env for local work; set the same names in
# Vercel (Project Settings -> Environment Variables) for production. Never commit real values.

# 1. PostgreSQL connection string (Vercel Postgres, Neon, Supabase, or a local database).
#    The app runs on this. For schema commands (npx prisma db push) use your provider's
#    direct / unpooled connection string instead.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://username:password@localhost:5432/rke"

# 2. Secret key that signs login cookies. Use 32 or more random characters,
#    for example:  openssl rand -base64 32
#    Changing it signs every user out.
SESSION_SECRET="your-random-session-secret-key-here"

# 3. Gemini API Key for Invoice OCR — primary reader (Free: https://aistudio.google.com).
#    It is the only reader that accepts PDF files. Without any AI key the scan button
#    simply reports that scanning is not set up. (Keys are commented out so a plain copy
#    of this file does not set fake ones.)
# GEMINI_API_KEY="AIzaSyYourGeminiApiKeyHere"

# 4. OpenAI API Key — fallback for pictures when Gemini is unavailable (https://platform.openai.com).
#    Used automatically when Gemini cannot answer. Set either or both fallbacks.
# OPENAI_API_KEY="sk-YourOpenAIKeyHere"

# 5. Mistral API Key — free tier fallback, no credit card required (https://console.mistral.ai).
# MISTRAL_API_KEY="YourMistralKeyHere"

# 6. Optional: choose the model each reader uses. Leave unset to use the defaults in lib/ocr.ts.
#    If a provider retires a model, set a current one here instead of changing the code.
# GEMINI_MODEL=""
# OPENAI_MODEL=""
# MISTRAL_MODEL=""

# 7. Optional: allow people to sign up. Sign-up is CLOSED unless this is set, and then
#    anyone who knows the code can create a login (new logins can use the AI scan keys above).
# SIGNUP_INVITE_CODE="a-code-you-share-only-with-people-you-trust"

# 8. First login, used only by:  npx prisma db seed
#    Nothing about a login is kept in the repository. The password needs 10+ characters.
#    An existing user is left alone unless SEED_RESET_PASSWORD="true".
# SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL="you@example.com"
# SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD="a long password"
# SEED_ADMIN_NAME="Your Name"
# SEED_RESET_PASSWORD="false"
